main.cpp
--cpp20
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ aggregate: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ member call: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ at offset 0: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ T: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ constructors of an empty member run: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.6\] line \d+ Holder: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.7\] line \d+ offsetof: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.8\] line \d+ pointer to member: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.9\] line \d+ destructor of an empty member runs: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.10\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
static assertion failed
could not be evaluated
--
The member had no zero-size layout before; this checks that its
initialization, aggregate initialization, member calls and decltype work
with the layout that gives it zero size.
Tagged itanium-abi: Visual Studio ignores [[no_unique_address]] (it has
[[msvc::no_unique_address]]), which [intro.object]/8 permits, and so does
cbmc's Visual Studio mode.
